    "narrative": "The Austin Waves front office has prioritized high-efficiency matchups for today\u2019s slate, anchored by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Jackson Merrill** (73.00), our top-scoring options. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** faces a favorable matchup against Wacha, benefiting from a significant 14% dynamic platoon boost and an optimal #2 spot in the order. Meanwhile, **Jackson Merrill** draws a standout profile; while the park factor is slightly suppressive, his ability to exploit Pallante\u2019s slow delivery\u2014driving a 100% stolen base expectation\u2014solidifies him as a cornerstone of our SB-focused strategy today. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (69.78) also provides a high floor, as the LHP Tolle allows us to leverage **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**\u2019s platoon edge, pushing him into the top tier of today\u2019s projected production.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the board was keeping **Miguel Vargas** (59.66) and **Gunnar Henderson** (58.38) on the bench. **Miguel Vargas** narrowly missed the final lineup spot; although he boasts a strong profile against Cole, he ultimately fell short of the threshold compared to the platoon-adjusted value offered by **Dominic Smith** and **Wade Meckler** in more favorable hitting environments. **Gunnar Henderson**, despite his pedigree, is facing the high-strikeout arm of Gilbert, which suppressed his SP skill score by 18%, forcing a cautious approach to maintain our game cap efficiency. We are closely monitoring weather reports for the **Kyle Tucker** matchup; his score is hampered by a significant SP skill penalty (15%) against Rasmussen, and while he remains in the lineup for his high base projection, his output is the most volatile among our starters should the weather in his park shift.",
